1
00:00:00,418 --> 00:00:01,707
<i>Previously on</i> Reacher...

2
00:00:01,711 --> 00:00:03,583
She sent Anna an address.

3
00:00:03,587 --> 00:00:05,419
[Russell] First floor is
an abandoned restaurant.

4
00:00:05,423 --> 00:00:07,254
{\an8}Looks like it's under
some kind of renovation.

5
00:00:07,258 --> 00:00:08,630
{\an8}[Reacher] <i>That's where
we're headed to next.</i>

6
00:00:08,634 --> 00:00:09,965
{\an8}-[glass shatters]
-[grunts]

7
00:00:09,969 --> 00:00:12,092
I got a GSW to the chest!

8
00:00:12,096 --> 00:00:13,677
Check in on Russell Plum.

9
00:00:13,681 --> 00:00:15,887
Tell him
I'm sorry I left him at the library.

10
00:00:15,891 --> 00:00:17,097
The night my sister died,

11
00:00:17,101 --> 00:00:20,267
<i>she had a jump drive
with a decades-old photo.</i>

12
00:00:20,271 --> 00:00:22,431
General Putra wants to take
a photo with the two of us.

13
00:00:22,690 --> 00:00:25,522
[Ahlquist] <i>The whiteboard was
in the background, out of focus.</i>

14
00:00:25,526 --> 00:00:28,984
Newly developed AI can essentially
refocus the lens.

15
00:00:28,988 --> 00:00:30,110
It's working.

16
00:00:30,114 --> 00:00:31,695
[Ahlquist] <i>It contains the formula</i>

17
00:00:31,699 --> 00:00:33,280
<i>for a chemical weapon
of mass destruction.</i>

18
00:00:33,284 --> 00:00:34,281
[groans]

19
00:00:34,285 --> 00:00:35,407
You send a suicide bomber

20
00:00:35,411 --> 00:00:37,617
<i>with that stuff strapped to him
into Times Square,</i>

21
00:00:37,621 --> 00:00:39,703
<i>he'll kill everyone
within a ten-block radius.</i>

22
00:00:39,707 --> 00:00:41,246
Make enough to kill thousands.

23
00:00:41,250 --> 00:00:43,749
Lila's auctioning off the drive
on the dark web

24
00:00:43,753 --> 00:00:45,000
at 10:00 a.m. tomorrow.

25
00:00:45,004 --> 00:00:47,252
They're gonna kill people tonight
to prove it works.

26
00:00:47,256 --> 00:00:49,963
When I said Delta hunted down
and took out General Putra,

27
00:00:49,967 --> 00:00:51,757
<i>I was the one who pulled the trigger.</i>

28
00:00:51,761 --> 00:00:54,680
<i>The woman calling herself Amisha
saw me do it.</i>

29
00:00:55,181 --> 00:00:56,970
<i>They're hitting here. Where are you?</i>

30
00:00:56,974 --> 00:00:58,054
This is happening now.

31
00:00:58,058 --> 00:00:59,347
Right now, they don't know we know.

32
00:00:59,351 --> 00:01:01,016
Our best chance is
to neutralize the attack.

33
00:01:01,020 --> 00:01:03,063
-How?
-[yelling]

34
00:01:04,064 --> 00:01:05,061
{\an8}[explosion]

35
00:01:05,065 --> 00:01:07,151
[people screaming]

36
00:01:10,905 --> 00:01:12,986
-[tense music playing]
<i>-[siren wailing]</i>

37
00:01:12,990 --> 00:01:15,155
<i>[people screaming]</i>

38
00:01:15,159 --> 00:01:17,157
[shouting indistinctly]

39
00:01:17,161 --> 00:01:19,580
-[glass shatters]
-[screaming continues]

40
00:01:23,375 --> 00:01:24,790
-[security guard] Freeze, asshole!
-[gun slide racks]

41
00:01:24,794 --> 00:01:26,500
-Don't fucking move!
-[horn honking]

42
00:01:26,504 --> 00:01:28,084
[tires screeching]

43
00:01:28,088 --> 00:01:29,044
Get in!

44
00:01:29,048 --> 00:01:30,670
[exciting music playing]

45
00:01:30,674 --> 00:01:32,218
[Reacher] Go! [grunts]

46
00:01:32,551 --> 00:01:34,053
[gunshots]

47
00:01:35,471 --> 00:01:36,968
[bullets thudding into van]

48
00:01:36,972 --> 00:01:38,303
What the hell happened?

49
00:01:38,307 --> 00:01:40,347
Sampson tackled the bomber into the river.

50
00:01:40,351 --> 00:01:42,645
The water stopped the toxin
from aerosolizing.

51
00:01:43,813 --> 00:01:44,772
Sampson's dead.

52
00:01:45,523 --> 00:01:46,520
Shit.

53
00:01:46,524 --> 00:01:48,230
He saved a lot of lives.

54
00:01:48,234 --> 00:01:49,314
[Reacher] Temporarily.

55
00:01:49,318 --> 00:01:51,441
No one's gonna buy that bomb
unless they see that it works.

56
00:01:51,445 --> 00:01:53,360
Lila and Amisha will try again.

57
00:01:53,364 --> 00:01:54,694
And we have no idea where.

58
00:01:54,698 --> 00:01:56,534
Tomorrow's morning commute,
like we thought.

59
00:01:57,243 --> 00:01:58,990
Maybe something else.

60
00:01:58,994 --> 00:02:00,826
I don't know, but it's gonna happen soon.

61
00:02:00,830 --> 00:02:02,494
We have to tell someone.

62
00:02:02,498 --> 00:02:04,704
Who? They're gonna blame us for this.

63
00:02:04,708 --> 00:02:05,914
We're at the site of the bombing

64
00:02:05,918 --> 00:02:07,791
and then take off in a van
after we sent all those cops

65
00:02:07,795 --> 00:02:08,875
to the concert for nothing?

66
00:02:08,879 --> 00:02:10,752
They're gonna think
we did that as a distraction.

67
00:02:10,756 --> 00:02:12,212
We got to ditch this van.

68
00:02:12,216 --> 00:02:14,172
[suspenseful music playing]

69
00:02:14,176 --> 00:02:15,757
Find me a busy restaurant.

70
00:02:15,761 --> 00:02:18,472
-[horn honks]
-[horn honks]

71
00:02:19,473 --> 00:02:21,555
-[indistinct chatter]
-[siren wailing]

72
00:02:21,559 --> 00:02:23,599
-[indistinct radio chatter]
-[helicopter whirring]

73
00:02:25,062 --> 00:02:28,228
Ma'am, we're gonna need
to get you out of here

74
00:02:28,232 --> 00:02:29,896
in case of a second attack.

75
00:02:29,900 --> 00:02:31,902
[melancholy music playing]

76
00:02:34,613 --> 00:02:36,448
There was a crew
shooting video of the event.

77
00:02:37,575 --> 00:02:39,994
I want to see every frame
before the police get ahold of it.

78
00:02:42,371 --> 00:02:45,207
We don't know who we can trust,
and I'm not gonna let anyone bury this.

79
00:02:48,043 --> 00:02:49,712
We're gonna find who killed John...

80
00:02:52,006 --> 00:02:53,966
and we're gonna make them fucking pay.

81
00:03:09,481 --> 00:03:10,608
[car alarm chirps]

82
00:03:14,111 --> 00:03:15,525
[Tamara] <i>It's been too long.</i>

83
00:03:15,529 --> 00:03:16,947
I don't like him doing this.

84
00:03:18,240 --> 00:03:19,909
He's least likely to draw attention.

85
00:03:20,868 --> 00:03:22,657
He's small-town, but he's capable.

86
00:03:22,661 --> 00:03:24,910
You know he intends
to kill Lila and Amisha,

87
00:03:24,914 --> 00:03:26,536
or whatever the hell
their names really are.

88
00:03:26,540 --> 00:03:27,954
Good.

89
00:03:27,958 --> 00:03:29,293
Better world without 'em.

90
00:03:30,502 --> 00:03:32,709
Yeah, well...

91
00:03:32,713 --> 00:03:34,878
it's hard to go back to Mayfield
after you body someone,

92
00:03:34,882 --> 00:03:36,379
even if they deserve it.

93
00:03:36,383 --> 00:03:38,010
They already killed Anna and Ben.

94
00:03:38,886 --> 00:03:40,342
They shouldn't get to take his life, too.

95
00:03:40,346 --> 00:03:42,177
I didn't want him involved
in the first place.

96
00:03:42,181 --> 00:03:43,474
[vehicle approaches]

97
00:03:44,016 --> 00:03:44,934
[Reacher] That's him.

98
00:03:54,777 --> 00:03:55,982
Good choice.

99
00:03:55,986 --> 00:03:58,443
Popular car, dark color.

100
00:03:58,447 --> 00:03:59,527
We won't stand out.

101
00:03:59,531 --> 00:04:01,780
So glad I'm a good car thief.

102
00:04:01,784 --> 00:04:02,743
[Reacher] Head to D.C.

103
00:04:04,119 --> 00:04:06,242
-Plum's loft?
-Feds and local cops will have

104
00:04:06,246 --> 00:04:07,702
pulled the place apart by now.

105
00:04:07,706 --> 00:04:10,330
Plum's in the hospital.
We'd have no reason to go back.

106
00:04:10,334 --> 00:04:11,998
Last place anyone would look.

107
00:04:12,002 --> 00:04:13,792
Keep it under 70.

108
00:04:13,796 --> 00:04:15,710
We get pulled over, we have a problem.

109
00:04:15,714 --> 00:04:16,715
Copy that.

110
00:04:23,055 --> 00:04:25,261
[weatherman] <i>...multiple inches
of rain per hour,</i>

111
00:04:25,265 --> 00:04:27,639
<i>with even heavier downpours overnight.</i>

112
00:04:27,643 --> 00:04:30,308
<i>We're also tracking
a high number of lightning strikes</i>

113
00:04:30,312 --> 00:04:32,394
<i>within the leading edge of the system,</i>

114
00:04:32,398 --> 00:04:33,895
<i>and that's expected to increase</i>

115
00:04:33,899 --> 00:04:35,814
<i>as the storm approaches the city.</i>

116
00:04:35,818 --> 00:04:37,482
-[groans]
<i>-We'll continue updating this</i>

117
00:04:37,486 --> 00:04:39,067
<i>throughout the evening, so keep it here</i>

118
00:04:39,071 --> 00:04:42,821
<i>as we track tonight's
unseasonably strong summer storm.</i>

119
00:04:42,825 --> 00:04:44,531
-[news program theme plays]
-Oh, shit.

120
00:04:44,535 --> 00:04:46,324
[news anchor] <i>Just in,
we have more on the attack</i>

121
00:04:46,328 --> 00:04:48,159
<i>that killed North Carolina representative</i>

122
00:04:48,163 --> 00:04:52,163
<i>and recently-announced
presidential candidate John Sampson.</i>

123
00:04:52,167 --> 00:04:54,332
-Shit.
<i>-A camera crew covering</i>

124
00:04:54,336 --> 00:04:56,918
<i>the Feed America event at the waterfront</i>

125
00:04:56,922 --> 00:04:58,461
<i>caught this footage</i>

126
00:04:58,465 --> 00:04:59,671
<i>-of Congressman Sampson...</i>
-[straining]

127
00:04:59,675 --> 00:05:02,716
<i>tackling the suicide bomber
into the water...</i>

128
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:04,467
-[grunts in relief]
<i>-Sacrificing himself</i>

129
00:05:04,471 --> 00:05:06,344
<i>to save countless lives.</i>

130
00:05:06,348 --> 00:05:09,139
<i>We caution that
this footage is disturbing.</i>

131
00:05:09,143 --> 00:05:10,682
<i>[indistinct chatter]</i>

132
00:05:10,686 --> 00:05:12,813
<i>[Sampson yelling]</i>

133
00:05:13,522 --> 00:05:14,477
<i>[loud splash]</i>

134
00:05:14,481 --> 00:05:15,437
<i>[explosion]</i>

135
00:05:15,441 --> 00:05:17,105
<i>[people screaming]</i>

136
00:05:17,109 --> 00:05:19,482
[news anchor] <i>Congressman Sampson's
widow, Elspeth Sampson,</i>

137
00:05:19,486 --> 00:05:21,693
<i>is asking that anyone with information</i>

138
00:05:21,697 --> 00:05:24,571
<i>about this man, or his accomplices,</i>

139
00:05:24,575 --> 00:05:26,322
<i>to please reach out directly</i>

140
00:05:26,326 --> 00:05:29,659
<i>to Congressman Sampson's
head of security at this number.</i>

141
00:05:29,663 --> 00:05:31,411
[tense, percussive music playing]

142
00:05:31,415 --> 00:05:33,125
"Tomas Waberi."

143
00:05:34,501 --> 00:05:36,628
[groaning softly]

144
00:05:45,137 --> 00:05:46,638
[straining]

145
00:05:49,767 --> 00:05:52,227
[panting]

146
00:05:53,520 --> 00:05:54,772
-[groaning]
-[monitor beeping]

147
00:05:56,190 --> 00:05:58,438
[panting]

148
00:05:58,442 --> 00:06:00,527
[groaning]

149
00:06:06,075 --> 00:06:07,367
Oh...

150
00:06:10,621 --> 00:06:11,705
Okay.

151
00:06:13,165 --> 00:06:14,746
[groans]

152
00:06:14,750 --> 00:06:15,872
[yells]

153
00:06:15,876 --> 00:06:16,877
Shit.

154
00:06:18,295 --> 00:06:19,338
Okay.

155
00:06:21,882 --> 00:06:23,046
[groans softly]

156
00:06:23,050 --> 00:06:24,551
[panting]

157
00:06:26,303 --> 00:06:28,180
[grunts, yells]

158
00:06:29,264 --> 00:06:30,720
[groaning]

159
00:06:30,724 --> 00:06:31,888
The fuck?

160
00:06:31,892 --> 00:06:33,139
Excuse me.

161
00:06:33,143 --> 00:06:34,808
Help me to get him into bed.

162
00:06:34,812 --> 00:06:36,768
[Russell groaning loudly]

163
00:06:36,772 --> 00:06:38,978
You just had surgery.
What in God's name

164
00:06:38,982 --> 00:06:41,276
-were you trying to do?
-[groaning]

165
00:06:49,535 --> 00:06:50,532
Who you trying to call?

166
00:06:50,536 --> 00:06:51,825
[groans]

167
00:06:51,829 --> 00:06:53,785
[panting]

168
00:06:53,789 --> 00:06:55,453
[Docherty] I ain't on
the wrong side of all this.

169
00:06:55,457 --> 00:06:58,581
Jacob Merrick asked me
to come here and check on you.

170
00:06:58,585 --> 00:07:00,750
He said he's sorry
he left you at the library,

171
00:07:00,754 --> 00:07:02,836
whatever the fuck that means.

172
00:07:02,840 --> 00:07:04,212
What's going on?

173
00:07:04,216 --> 00:07:06,005
[labored breathing]

174
00:07:06,009 --> 00:07:08,174
[faintly] Tomas... Waberi.

175
00:07:08,178 --> 00:07:09,509
You were trying to call him?

176
00:07:09,513 --> 00:07:11,928
No. That's...

177
00:07:11,932 --> 00:07:14,430
the suici... [wheezes]

178
00:07:14,434 --> 00:07:15,890
Suicide bomber.

179
00:07:15,894 --> 00:07:18,726
[groaning]

180
00:07:18,730 --> 00:07:19,894
Are you sure about that?

181
00:07:19,898 --> 00:07:21,020
I'm sure.

182
00:07:21,024 --> 00:07:22,313
I'm s... [groans]

183
00:07:22,317 --> 00:07:23,314
[Docherty] Okay.

184
00:07:23,318 --> 00:07:24,862
{\an8}-I'll take it from here.
-Okay.

185
00:07:25,904 --> 00:07:27,402
You did good, Plum.

186
00:07:27,406 --> 00:07:28,361
[Russell exhales]

187
00:07:28,365 --> 00:07:30,742
[whimpers, groans]

188
00:07:34,246 --> 00:07:36,327
[intense music playing]

189
00:07:36,331 --> 00:07:38,167
[sirens wailing]

190
00:07:42,546 --> 00:07:43,672
[SWAT officer] Clear!

191
00:07:45,257 --> 00:07:46,379
[SWAT officer 2] Clear!

192
00:07:46,383 --> 00:07:47,797
-[SWAT officer 3] Clear!
-Damn.

193
00:07:47,801 --> 00:07:48,923
[SWAT officer 4] Clear!

194
00:07:48,927 --> 00:07:50,091
[SWAT officer] Clear!

195
00:07:50,095 --> 00:07:52,014
[indistinct radio chatter]

196
00:07:53,265 --> 00:07:54,808
Shit.

197
00:07:58,312 --> 00:08:00,314
<i>[phone ringing]</i>

198
00:08:03,609 --> 00:08:04,856
Docherty, what up?

199
00:08:04,860 --> 00:08:07,650
Your boy Plum pointed us
to the guy who killed Sampson.

200
00:08:07,654 --> 00:08:08,902
Russell's okay?

201
00:08:08,906 --> 00:08:10,945
He's jacked up, but alive.

202
00:08:10,949 --> 00:08:12,447
<i>Nearly ripped himself apart</i>

203
00:08:12,451 --> 00:08:15,366
trying to get us the name of the bomber,
Tomas Waberi.

204
00:08:15,370 --> 00:08:17,827
<i>Now, we ran it down.
He rented a car when he landed.</i>

205
00:08:17,831 --> 00:08:21,581
Rental agency used GPS
to trace it to a warehouse.

206
00:08:21,585 --> 00:08:24,209
Car was in the lot, but place was empty.

207
00:08:24,213 --> 00:08:25,793
<i>Only thing they left behind was</i>

208
00:08:25,797 --> 00:08:28,004
a sealed, 45-gallon drum

209
00:08:28,008 --> 00:08:29,589
with a dead kid inside.

210
00:08:29,593 --> 00:08:31,299
<i>Never seen anything like it.</i>

211
00:08:31,303 --> 00:08:32,967
They tested the toxin on him.

212
00:08:32,971 --> 00:08:34,677
Anything pointing to where they went?

213
00:08:34,681 --> 00:08:38,014
Credit card that bought
Waberi's plane ticket picked up 13 more

214
00:08:38,018 --> 00:08:39,807
for a red-eye tonight,

215
00:08:39,811 --> 00:08:42,227
<i>two first class, 11 coach.</i>

216
00:08:42,231 --> 00:08:43,649
Lila and Amisha are first class.

217
00:08:44,483 --> 00:08:46,439
The other 11,
figure a computer expert,

218
00:08:46,443 --> 00:08:49,567
a chemist,
maybe an explosives guy to rig the vest.

219
00:08:49,571 --> 00:08:51,152
The rest are trained killers.

220
00:08:51,156 --> 00:08:53,321
Reinforcements brought in
when things went to hell.

221
00:08:53,325 --> 00:08:55,698
[Docherty] <i>Well, we're tracking down
the names they'll be flying under.</i>

222
00:08:55,702 --> 00:08:57,659
It's gonna be all hands on deck at PHL.

223
00:08:57,663 --> 00:08:58,622
They won't show.

224
00:08:59,456 --> 00:09:01,329
-Why not?
-'Cause the attack failed.

225
00:09:01,333 --> 00:09:03,748
They didn't prove to bidders
their chemical weapon works.

226
00:09:03,752 --> 00:09:06,042
Tell that to fish in the Delaware.

227
00:09:06,046 --> 00:09:08,294
Better yet, tell that to John Sampson.

228
00:09:08,298 --> 00:09:10,755
Trust me,
these assholes proved their point.

229
00:09:10,759 --> 00:09:12,757
Their point was to demonstrate
a chemical weapon

230
00:09:12,761 --> 00:09:14,926
that's effectively lethal outdoors.

231
00:09:14,930 --> 00:09:16,177
They aren't going anywhere.

232
00:09:16,181 --> 00:09:17,762
[Docherty] <i>They got what they came for.</i>

233
00:09:17,766 --> 00:09:20,435
All that's left for them is
to get out of Dodge and cash in.

234
00:09:21,144 --> 00:09:23,017
When they arrive at the airport,
we'll be waiting.

235
00:09:23,021 --> 00:09:25,979
Just keep your heads down
until we got 'em in custody.

236
00:09:25,983 --> 00:09:28,564
<i>You were there
when a congressman exploded.</i>

237
00:09:28,568 --> 00:09:30,858
Everyone thinks you're working with 'em.

238
00:09:30,862 --> 00:09:32,698
-Don't be a fucking hero.
-[phone beeps off]

239
00:09:37,661 --> 00:09:39,909
Are you 100% on Lila
and Amisha not running off?

240
00:09:39,913 --> 00:09:40,910
Pretty much.

241
00:09:40,914 --> 00:09:42,287
Well, we need to find them,

242
00:09:42,291 --> 00:09:43,538
'cause the cops aren't looking.

243
00:09:43,542 --> 00:09:44,918
They could be anywhere.

244
00:09:46,420 --> 00:09:48,042
Not anywhere.

245
00:09:48,046 --> 00:09:49,711
They need somewhere
they can cook the poison.

246
00:09:49,715 --> 00:09:51,754
Somewhere they can pivot to quickly,

247
00:09:51,758 --> 00:09:53,464
a place no one would think they'd go.

248
00:09:53,468 --> 00:09:54,590
[tense music playing]

249
00:09:54,594 --> 00:09:55,637
Fuck.

250
00:09:57,347 --> 00:09:58,970
They're doing what we're doing.

251
00:09:58,974 --> 00:10:00,814
Circling back to where
the cops already looked.

252
00:10:02,060 --> 00:10:03,599
The vacant restaurant building?

253
00:10:03,603 --> 00:10:04,976
Turn around.

254
