everybody now...</i>

526
00:33:41,812 --> 00:33:43,518
We should go get that.

527
00:33:43,522 --> 00:33:45,895
<i>♪ Let me see your hands up,
everybody now, let me see ♪</i>

528
00:33:45,899 --> 00:33:47,814
-Yeah.
-<i>♪ your hands up, right now, hands up ♪</i>

529
00:33:47,818 --> 00:33:49,820
[tense, dark music playing]

530
00:33:52,156 --> 00:33:54,158
[thunder crashes]

531
00:34:03,751 --> 00:34:06,295
[breathing heavily]

532
00:34:10,591 --> 00:34:12,593
[panting]

533
00:34:38,911 --> 00:34:40,913
♪♪

534
00:34:44,750 --> 00:34:46,084
[gun clatters on floor]

535
00:35:01,183 --> 00:35:02,684
[footsteps approaching]

536
00:35:03,727 --> 00:35:05,729
[shoes squeaking on tile]

537
00:35:06,980 --> 00:35:08,899
[panting]

538
00:35:34,299 --> 00:35:35,797
[grunts]

539
00:35:35,801 --> 00:35:37,465
[groans]

540
00:35:37,469 --> 00:35:39,471
[panting]

541
00:35:48,647 --> 00:35:50,482
[yells, grunts]

542
00:36:07,958 --> 00:36:09,622
-Ah!
-[grunts]

543
00:36:09,626 --> 00:36:12,584
[grunting]

544
00:36:12,588 --> 00:36:15,420
I don't know what I enjoy more,

545
00:36:15,424 --> 00:36:17,714
fucking you or killing you.

546
00:36:17,718 --> 00:36:19,177
[grunting]

547
00:36:41,283 --> 00:36:43,827
I know which one I like more.

548
00:36:46,038 --> 00:36:47,623
[Reacher grunts]

549
00:36:49,082 --> 00:36:51,209
[panting]

550
00:37:04,306 --> 00:37:06,391
-[rain falling heavily]
-[sighs]

551
00:37:09,061 --> 00:37:10,270
[groans]

552
00:37:15,192 --> 00:37:16,731
[grunts]

553
00:37:16,735 --> 00:37:18,737
[breathing heavily]

554
00:37:27,204 --> 00:37:29,285
[thunder rolling]

555
00:37:29,289 --> 00:37:30,624
-[thunder crashes]
-[exhales]

556
00:37:35,170 --> 00:37:37,172
[somber music playing]

557
00:37:38,674 --> 00:37:39,841
Ah.

558
00:37:46,181 --> 00:37:47,599
Ah.

559
00:37:49,184 --> 00:37:52,020
[panting]

560
00:37:55,691 --> 00:37:58,022
[grunting]

561
00:37:58,026 --> 00:37:59,528
[groaning]

562
00:38:15,627 --> 00:38:17,629
♪♪

563
00:38:31,435 --> 00:38:34,187
[Foster] I am goddamn impressed, Reacher.

564
00:38:35,272 --> 00:38:37,691
Assume you killed everyone in there?

565
00:38:39,985 --> 00:38:42,316
Looks like they got a few licks
of their own in, too.

566
00:38:42,320 --> 00:38:43,697
[groans]

567
00:38:51,204 --> 00:38:52,664
[gasps]

568
00:38:56,043 --> 00:38:57,461
Surprised to see me?

569
00:38:59,755 --> 00:39:01,506
After our last run-in...

570
00:39:03,133 --> 00:39:06,011
figured the smart thing to do
was to just...

571
00:39:07,763 --> 00:39:09,385
follow you around.

572
00:39:09,389 --> 00:39:11,516
Wait for you to bring the drive to me.

573
00:39:17,981 --> 00:39:19,733
Thanks for taking care of the hard part.

574
00:39:24,654 --> 00:39:26,865
[dark music playing]

575
00:39:33,246 --> 00:39:34,790
[groans]

576
00:39:36,249 --> 00:39:37,751
[yells, screams]

577
00:39:41,797 --> 00:39:43,461
[exhales]

578
00:39:43,465 --> 00:39:45,509
♪♪

579
00:39:49,221 --> 00:39:51,636
{\an8}[Amisha groaning]

580
00:39:51,640 --> 00:39:52,849
{\an8}[groans]

581
00:39:58,730 --> 00:40:00,315
[panting]

582
00:40:14,913 --> 00:40:16,915
[straining]

583
00:40:21,878 --> 00:40:23,255
Ah!

584
00:40:36,643 --> 00:40:40,981
Your sister and nephew died
like cowards.

585
00:40:42,023 --> 00:40:43,813
I will not.

586
00:40:43,817 --> 00:40:46,027
Take it to hell!

587
00:40:58,373 --> 00:40:59,708
[groans]

588
00:41:11,011 --> 00:41:12,554
[exhales]

589
00:41:16,349 --> 00:41:18,727
You're under arrest for the murder...

590
00:41:20,562 --> 00:41:22,063
for the murder of John Sampson...

591
00:41:23,398 --> 00:41:25,609
Benjamin Merrick, and Anna Merrick.

592
00:41:27,235 --> 00:41:28,778
You have the right to remain silent.

593
00:41:29,571 --> 00:41:31,235
-[groans]
-And anything you say

594
00:41:31,239 --> 00:41:33,821
can and will be used against you

595
00:41:33,825 --> 00:41:35,114
in a court of law.

596
00:41:35,118 --> 00:41:37,495
You have the right to an attorney.

597
00:41:38,538 --> 00:41:40,745
{\an8}If you cannot afford one,

598
00:41:40,749 --> 00:41:42,538
{\an8}-one will be appointed to you.
-[sirens approaching]

599
00:41:42,542 --> 00:41:44,999
{\an8}If you decide to answer questions now...

600
00:41:45,003 --> 00:41:47,243
{\an8}-[Jacob continues indistinctly]
-[somber music playing]

601
00:41:53,386 --> 00:41:55,388
[birds singing]

602
00:41:59,935 --> 00:42:02,335
-[monitor beeping steadily]
-[indistinct P.A. announcement]

603
00:42:07,108 --> 00:42:08,568
[snores]

604
00:42:10,153 --> 00:42:11,655
[groans softly]

605
00:42:15,116 --> 00:42:16,117
[Reacher sighs]

606
00:42:18,078 --> 00:42:19,246
Uh...

607
00:42:20,705 --> 00:42:22,411
He's risen.

608
00:42:22,415 --> 00:42:24,247
Where's the drive?

609
00:42:24,251 --> 00:42:26,086
Look in your hand.

610
00:42:28,922 --> 00:42:31,587
You almost killed the paramedics
who tried to take it from you.

611
00:42:31,591 --> 00:42:33,547
Why aren't I cuffed?

612
00:42:33,551 --> 00:42:35,053
No charges.

613
00:42:35,720 --> 00:42:37,973
Lots of bodies can be traced back to me.

614
00:42:39,349 --> 00:42:41,305
My blood's all over that building.

615
00:42:41,309 --> 00:42:43,641
Sampson's widow's not to be
fucked with.

616
00:42:43,645 --> 00:42:45,851
DOD took charge of the scene,

617
00:42:45,855 --> 00:42:47,478
spun a whole story about a federal raid.

618
00:42:47,482 --> 00:42:48,604
Kept your name out of it.

619
00:42:48,608 --> 00:42:50,856
Figured you'd prefer it that way.

620
00:42:50,860 --> 00:42:52,191
I got some credit, though.

621
00:42:52,195 --> 00:42:53,405
So did Jacob.

622
00:42:55,240 --> 00:42:56,237
How is he?

623
00:42:56,241 --> 00:42:58,159
Okay, considering.

624
00:42:59,327 --> 00:43:01,909
Been trading shifts with me,
babysitting you.

625
00:43:01,913 --> 00:43:03,456
How about you?

626
00:43:04,416 --> 00:43:05,413
Truth?

627
00:43:05,417 --> 00:43:08,128
I think we're past the point
of lying to each other.

628
00:43:09,546 --> 00:43:11,047
Feel pretty good.

629
00:43:12,048 --> 00:43:13,800
Better than I have in a while.

630
00:43:15,427 --> 00:43:16,886
Think I'm ready to be a cop again.

631
00:43:17,595 --> 00:43:18,676
What about retirement?

632
00:43:18,680 --> 00:43:20,052
[chuckles]

633
00:43:20,056 --> 00:43:21,516
Ask me again in 20 years.

634
00:43:23,893 --> 00:43:25,312
[alarm sounds]

635
00:43:28,189 --> 00:43:29,228
What the hell are you doing?

636
00:43:29,232 --> 00:43:30,233
Leaving.

637
00:43:32,861 --> 00:43:34,567
Sir, what are you doing?

638
00:43:34,571 --> 00:43:35,776
Leaving.

639
00:43:35,780 --> 00:43:37,611
That's not the doctor's orders.

640
00:43:37,615 --> 00:43:40,031
I stopped taking orders
when I left the Army.

641
00:43:40,035 --> 00:43:42,078
I'm getting Dr. Newhook.

642
00:43:43,163 --> 00:43:44,247
Where are my clothes?

643
00:43:45,081 --> 00:43:46,871
Got you some new gear.

644
00:43:46,875 --> 00:43:49,582
New boots are on
that little table in the corner.

645
00:43:49,586 --> 00:43:52,339
Get dressed fast.
I don't need to see your ass.

646
00:43:54,507 --> 00:43:57,423
Doc said that big scar you had
saved your life.

647
00:43:57,427 --> 00:43:59,967
Thick scar tissue kept the blade shallow.

648
00:43:59,971 --> 00:44:01,771
Hadn't've been for that,
you wouldn't be here.

649
00:44:02,390 --> 00:44:03,554
Lucky me.

650
00:44:03,558 --> 00:44:04,434
[pants zip]

651
00:44:06,394 --> 00:44:07,562
[Tamara] Oh.

652
00:44:10,398 --> 00:44:12,855
Here's your sad little bag of shit
from when they arrested you.

653
00:44:12,859 --> 00:44:15,316
Passport, toothbrush,
burner phone, and cash.

654
00:44:15,320 --> 00:44:16,567
I threw in a few extra bucks.

655
00:44:16,571 --> 00:44:18,069
You're poor, Reacher.

656
00:44:18,073 --> 00:44:19,074
Thanks.

657
00:44:20,116 --> 00:44:21,489
But I need another favor.

658
00:44:21,493 --> 00:44:22,740
What?

659
00:44:22,744 --> 00:44:24,746
I want you to get something
back for me.

660
00:44:26,081 --> 00:44:28,079
{\an8}[meows]

661
00:44:28,083 --> 00:44:29,709
{\an8}-[purrs, meows]
-[busy chatter]

662
00:44:33,546 --> 00:44:35,461
Sir. Sir?

663
00:44:35,465 --> 00:44:37,296
You can't have that in here!

664
00:44:37,300 --> 00:44:38,843
[exhales]

665
00:44:39,344 --> 00:44:40,512
-Reacher.
-[kitten meowing]

666
00:44:41,179 --> 00:44:42,764
I brought you something.

667
00:44:44,265 --> 00:44:46,184
-He's yours now.
-What?

668
00:44:49,270 --> 00:44:50,768
Hey. [chuckles]

669
00:44:50,772 --> 00:44:51,852
[purring]

670
00:44:51,856 --> 00:44:54,150
I'm gonna call you Walter Cron-Cat.

671
00:44:56,069 --> 00:44:57,858
Man, you do not look so good.

672
00:44:57,862 --> 00:44:59,110
Neither do you.

673
00:44:59,114 --> 00:45:01,028
[laughs]

674
00:45:01,032 --> 00:45:03,781
You know, uh, Jacob and Tamara came by.

675
00:45:03,785 --> 00:45:05,120
They told me it was over.

676
00:45:06,204 --> 00:45:07,785
Not yet.

677
00:45:07,789 --> 00:45:10,509
I kept telling people I'd know
what I'd do with this when I found it.

678
00:45:12,877 --> 00:45:14,337
Write your story.

679
00:45:15,463 --> 00:45:16,877
Get your Pulitzer.

680
00:45:16,881 --> 00:45:18,963
[gentle music playing]

681
00:45:18,967 --> 00:45:20,969
[kitten continues purring]

682
00:45:24,431 --> 00:45:25,932
Take care of the cat, Plum.

683
00:45:27,308 --> 00:45:29,185
Take care of yourself, Reacher.

684
00:45:30,228 --> 00:45:31,392
Hey.

685
00:45:31,396 --> 00:45:34,858
I told you the pen was mightier
than the sword.

686
00:45:37,902 --> 00:45:39,696
Sword played its part, too.

687
00:45:44,242 --> 00:45:46,327
[phone ringing]

688
00:45:51,082 --> 00:45:52,083
Hello?

689
00:45:52,959 --> 00:45:53,960
Yes.

690
00:45:55,879 --> 00:45:57,501
I'll see you in 15 minutes.

691
00:45:57,505 --> 00:45:58,878
[phone beeps off]

692
00:45:58,882 --> 00:46:01,213
[birds singing]

693
00:46:01,217 --> 00:46:02,381
-[classical music playing]
-Cream and sugar?

694
00:46:02,385 --> 00:46:03,470
No, thanks.

695
00:46:04,179 --> 00:46:05,180
Me, neither.

696
00:46:06,306 --> 00:46:08,141
Cream and sugar's just gilding the lily.

697
00:46:09,517 --> 00:46:12,395
Thank you for meeting me here
on such short notice.

698
00:46:13,188 --> 00:46:15,311
Thank you for making sure
I won't face charges.

699
00:46:15,315 --> 00:46:18,151
It's amazing the good will
my husband's name carries now.

700
00:46:19,569 --> 00:46:22,401
All it took was him dying a hero.
[chuckles]

701
00:46:22,405 --> 00:46:25,492
Washington's mostly empty suits
spouting empty promises.

702
00:46:26,284 --> 00:46:27,744
Not many people there impress me.

703
00:46:28,745 --> 00:46:30,079
John Sampson did.

704
00:46:31,164 --> 00:46:32,536
So do you.

705
00:46:32,540 --> 00:46:34,501
That's nice to hear...

706
00:46:35,585 --> 00:46:38,004
since I'm considering
picking up his mantle.

707
00:46:39,130 --> 00:46:41,758
Two ethical politicians
from the same family.

708
00:46:42,717 --> 00:46:43,801
Who would've thought?

709
00:46:44,844 --> 00:46:46,509
Can I count on your vote?

710
00:46:46,513 --> 00:46:47,680
Not registered.

711
00:46:48,848 --> 00:46:50,058
No residence.

712
00:46:54,979 --> 00:46:57,478
So, Reacher...

713
00:46:57,482 --> 00:47:00,940
I guess
the only thing left to discuss is...

714
00:47:00,944 --> 00:47:02,487
where's the drive?

715
00:47:02,904 --> 00:47:04,072
Safe.

716
00:47:05,156 --> 00:47:06,908
But the story is gonna come out.

717
00:47:07,909 --> 00:47:08,910
Good.

718
00:47:09,911 --> 00:47:12,243
If my husband had known
what was going on back in '98,

719
00:47:12,247 --> 00:47:13,807
he'd have done something about it then.

720
00:47:14,123 --> 00:47:16,121
I don't think he'd want
the truth buried now.

721
00:47:16,125 --> 00:47:18,002
That's why he would've been
a great president.

722
00:47:19,420 --> 00:47:20,797
You could be, too.

723
00:47:23,550 --> 00:47:24,672
Reacher.

724
00:47:24,676 --> 00:47:26,006
Springfield.

725
00:47:26,010 --> 00:47:28,384
Ma'am, reporter's here
to speak with you.

726
00:47:28,388 --> 00:47:29,760
Okay. Thank you.

727
00:47:29,764 --> 00:47:31,182
I'll leave you to it.

728
00:47:33,059 --> 00:47:34,394
Can we give you a ride?

729
00:47:36,062 --> 00:47:37,438
You could.

730
00:47:41,484 --> 00:47:42,940
[exhales]

731
00:47:42,944 --> 00:47:44,946
[luggage cart rattles]

732
00:47:46,906 --> 00:47:48,908
[quiet chatter]

733
00:47:51,703 --> 00:47:52,996
You fellas waiting for me?

734
00:47:53,705 --> 00:47:57,162
Our bosses sent some B-team boys
over to do a debriefing with you.

735
00:47:57,166 --> 00:47:58,998
That's not gonna happen, is it?

736
00:47:59,002 --> 00:48:00,044
Nope.

737
00:48:00,753 --> 00:48:02,501
Look, can you just do us one solid?

738
00:48:02,505 --> 00:48:04,628
We just need to put
a little check in a little box

739
00:48:04,632 --> 00:48:07,214
that says we asked you
one very specific question.

740
00:48:07,218 --> 00:48:08,303
Ask.

741
00:48:08,928 --> 00:48:11,260
Did you receive or
come into possession of a jump drive

742
00:48:11,264 --> 00:48:13,262
at any time during your final interactions

743
00:48:13,266 --> 00:48:17,141
with the two women operating under
the aliases Lila and Amisha Hoth?

744
00:48:17,145 --> 00:48:19,184
[tense, atmospheric music playing]

745
00:48:19,188 --> 00:48:20,315
No.

746
00:48:23,359 --> 00:48:24,611
Good enough.

747
00:48:27,864 --> 00:48:30,571
Thank you for what you did
for the country, Reacher.

748
00:48:30,575 --> 00:48:32,448
You're welcome...

749
00:48:32,452 --> 00:48:33,449
McMicheals.

750
00:48:33,453 --> 00:48:35,121
McMicheals.

751
00:48:36,664 --> 00:48:37,915
Jarvis.

752
00:48:38,916 --> 00:48:39,913
Thank you.

753
00:48:39,917 --> 00:48:41,127
You're welcome, Jarvis.

754
00:48:42,170 --> 00:48:44,251
Buhner. Thanks, Reacher.

755
00:48:44,255 --> 00:48:45,175
You're welcome, Buhner.

756
00:48:48,176 --> 00:48:49,135
[Reacher] Oh.

757
00:48:52,138 --> 00:48:53,431
Stay on the B-team.

758
00:48:54,223 --> 00:48:55,391
They don't get shot at.

759
00:48:58,936 --> 00:49:00,938
[♪ Mondo Cozmo singing "Sweet Forever"]

760
00:49:12,867 --> 00:49:16,829
<i>♪ I pulled myself
to the river's edge, man ♪</i>

761
00:49:19,248 --> 00:49:22,752
<i>♪ I was looking for some sweet relief ♪</i>

762
00:49:26,214 --> 00:49:29,546
<i>♪ And please forgive me for not knowing ♪</i>

763
00:49:29,550 --> 00:49:31,632
So you can be together forever.

764
00:49:31,636 --> 00:49:35,969
<i>♪ But I don't have the means ♪</i>

765
00:49:35,973 --> 00:49:39,390
<i>♪ I can sing it to ya in my sleep,
it goes ♪</i>

766
00:49:39,394 --> 00:49:43,189
<i>♪ Sweet forever ♪</i>

767
00:49:44,691 --> 00:49:49,153
<i>♪ Hallelujah till the end ♪</i>

768
00:49:51,322 --> 00:49:52,736
<i>♪ And it's a ♪</i>

769
00:49:52,740 --> 00:49:57,370
<i>♪ sweet surrender ♪</i>

770
00:49:58,121 --> 00:49:59,618
<i>♪ Until ♪</i>

771
00:49:59,622 --> 00:50:02,166
<i>♪ we meet again ♪</i>

772
00:50:04,794 --> 00:50:08,631
<i>♪ Until we meet again ♪</i>

773
00:50:34,031 --> 00:50:37,994
<i>♪ I pulled myself into
that River Thames, yeah...</i>

774
00:50:39,746 --> 00:50:40,909
[meows]

775
00:50:40,913 --> 00:50:43,912
[captain] <i>For action
above and beyond the call of duty,</i>

776
00:50:43,916 --> 00:50:47,791
it is my honor to present Tamara Green

777
00:50:47,795 --> 00:50:49,960
with the Philadelphia Police Department's

778
00:50:49,964 --> 00:50:54,715
Sergeant Robert Wilson III
Medal of Valor.

779
00:50:54,719 --> 00:50:57,346
[applause]

780
00:50:58,139 --> 00:51:00,345
It is also my great privilege

781
00:51:00,349 --> 00:51:03,223
to immediately reassign you
to Detective,

782
00:51:03,227 --> 00:51:04,979
Homicide Division.

783
00:51:08,566 --> 00:51:11,106
[cheering]

784
00:51:11,110 --> 00:51:13,317
She deserves it, you know? About time.

785
00:51:13,321 --> 00:51:14,568
Finally.

786
00:51:14,572 --> 00:51:17,321
<i>♪ Sweet surrender...</i>

787
00:51:17,325 --> 00:51:18,489
[commander] Fire!

788
00:51:18,493 --> 00:51:20,657
Ready! Aim!

789
00:51:20,661 --> 00:51:21,742
Fire!

790
00:51:21,746 --> 00:51:23,247
<i>♪ We meet again ♪</i>

791
00:51:26,209 --> 00:51:29,670
<i>♪ Until we meet again ♪</i>

792
00:51:32,340 --> 00:51:36,093
<i>♪ Until we meet again ♪</i>

793
00:51:38,888 --> 00:51:40,844
Whiz Wit.

794
00:51:40,848 --> 00:51:42,850
♪♪

795
00:52:01,744 --> 00:52:05,706
<i>♪ I pulled myself into
